# ArduCopter SITL parameters for the Arrow Air Quiver Dev-Kit: sim_vehicle.py -v ArduCopter -f quad --model JSON:<host> --add-param-file=<this>.
# Arrow's own standard-params.param (Arrow-air/project-quiver a14970474c, 2026-06-17), with only what SITL cannot have taken out
# or replaced; every change says why. With --model JSON current ArduPilot loads no frame defaults, so the file is self-contained.
# Names as ArduCopter 4.8-dev (b7ba8bca) spells them. 4.7 moved the cm and cdeg parameters to m and deg (x 0.01, the factor of
# its own conversion), so a line whose name differs from theirs carries their original above it.

AHRS_EKF_TYPE 3
AHRS_GPS_GAIN 1
AHRS_GPS_MINSATS 6
AHRS_GPS_USE 1
AHRS_OPTIONS 0
AHRS_ORIENTATION 0
AHRS_RP_P 0.2
AHRS_YAW_P 0.2
ARMING_ACCTHRESH 0.75
# ARMING_CHECK 1 (all checks) is ARMING_SKIPCHK 0 since 4.7, which is the default.
ARMING_MAGTHRESH 100
ARMING_NEED_LOC 0
ARMING_OPTIONS 0
ARMING_RUDDER 2

# Their attitude tune, as published.
# Theirs: ANGLE_MAX 3000, ATC_ACCEL_P_MAX 68443.15, ATC_ACCEL_R_MAX 60184.69, ATC_ACCEL_Y_MAX 9049, ATC_SLEW_YAW 6000
ATC_ANGLE_MAX 30
ATC_ACC_P_MAX 684.4315
ATC_ACC_R_MAX 601.8469
ATC_ACC_Y_MAX 90.49
ATC_RATE_WPY_MAX 60
ATC_ANG_LIM_TC 1
ATC_ANG_PIT_P 10.68668
ATC_ANG_RLL_P 11.33392
ATC_ANG_YAW_P 3.538
ATC_ANGLE_BOOST 1
ATC_INPUT_TC 0.15
ATC_RAT_PIT_D 0.009356325
ATC_RAT_PIT_FLTD 10
ATC_RAT_PIT_FLTT 10
ATC_RAT_PIT_I 0.1453998
ATC_RAT_PIT_IMAX 0.5
ATC_RAT_PIT_P 0.1453998
ATC_RAT_PIT_SMAX 50
ATC_RAT_RLL_D 0.009198768
ATC_RAT_RLL_FLTD 10
ATC_RAT_RLL_FLTT 10
ATC_RAT_RLL_I 0.142759
ATC_RAT_RLL_IMAX 0.5
ATC_RAT_RLL_P 0.142759
ATC_RAT_RLL_SMAX 50
ATC_RAT_YAW_D 0.01000001
ATC_RAT_YAW_FLTD 10
ATC_RAT_YAW_FLTE 2
ATC_RAT_YAW_FLTT 10
ATC_RAT_YAW_I 0.16
ATC_RAT_YAW_IMAX 0.5
ATC_RAT_YAW_P 1.6
ATC_RAT_YAW_SMAX 50
ATC_RATE_FF_ENAB 1
ATC_RATE_Y_MAX 30
ATC_THR_MIX_MAN 0.1
ATC_THR_MIX_MAX 0.5
ATC_THR_MIX_MIN 0.1
AVOID_ENABLE 0

# Battery: theirs is a Tattu 14S smart pack on DroneCAN (BATT_MONITOR 9). SITL's analog monitor reads the simulated pack instead:
# PteroSim sends the pack's terminal volts and amps as JSON "battery" (SIM_JSON.h:163-164), SITL puts them on pins 13/12 at
# /10.1 and /17 (SITL_State_common.cpp:494-495), and these multipliers read them back. SIM_BATT_VOLTAGE is only the fallback for
# a frame without battery: 0 refuses arming instead of reporting a pack that is not there.
SIM_BATT_VOLTAGE 0
BATT_MONITOR 4
BATT_VOLT_PIN 13
BATT_CURR_PIN 12
BATT_VOLT_MULT 10.1
BATT_AMP_PERVLT 17
BATT_AMP_OFFSET 0
BATT_ARM_VOLT 47.5
BATT_CAPACITY 30000
BATT_CRT_VOLT 44.8
# Theirs sets 48 on BATT2 and leaves BATT_LOW_VOLT at the copter default 10.5, below BATT_CRT_VOLT: arming refuses that
# ("voltage failsafe critical >= low"). SITL has one pack, so their low threshold goes on it.
BATT_LOW_VOLT 48
BATT_FS_CRT_ACT 1
BATT_FS_LOW_ACT 2
BATT_FS_VOLTSRC 1

DISARM_DELAY 10
EK3_ENABLE 1
EK3_ERR_THRESH 0.2
EK3_GPS_CHECK 31
EK3_IMU_MASK 3
EK3_MAG_CAL 3
EK3_PRIMARY 0
EK3_SRC_OPTIONS 1
EK3_SRC1_POSXY 3
EK3_SRC1_POSZ 1
EK3_SRC1_VELXY 3
EK3_SRC1_VELZ 3
EK3_SRC1_YAW 1
FENCE_ACTION 1
FENCE_ALT_MAX 30
FENCE_ALT_MIN -10
FENCE_ENABLE 1
FENCE_MARGIN 5
FENCE_RADIUS 60
FENCE_TYPE 7
FRAME_CLASS 1
FRAME_TYPE 1
FS_CRASH_CHECK 1
FS_DR_ENABLE 2
FS_DR_TIMEOUT 30
FS_EKF_ACTION 1
FS_EKF_FILT 5
FS_EKF_THRESH 0.8
FS_GCS_ENABLE 1
FS_GCS_TIMEOUT 5
FS_OPTIONS 16
FS_THR_ENABLE 1
FS_THR_VALUE 975
FS_VIBE_ENABLE 1

# GPS: theirs are two DroneCAN receivers (GPS1/2_TYPE 9). SITL simulates one serial u-blox on SERIAL3 (SITL_State.h _serial_path "GPS1").
GPS_AUTO_CONFIG 2
GPS_BLEND_MASK 5
GPS_HDOP_GOOD 160
GPS_MIN_ELEV 13
GPS_NAVFILTER 8
GPS_PRIMARY 0
GPS_SAVE_CFG 1
GPS1_GNSS_MODE 77
GPS1_RATE_MS 200
GPS1_TYPE 1
SERIAL3_PROTOCOL 5

# SITL's own accelerometer calibration (Tools/autotest/default_params/copter.parm), which a JSON run never loads: offsets of
# exactly zero read as uncalibrated ("3D Accel calibration needed"). SITL simulates two IMUs (SIM_IMU_COUNT 2).
INS_ACCOFFS_X 0.001
INS_ACCOFFS_Y 0.001
INS_ACCOFFS_Z 0.001
INS_ACCSCAL_X 1.001
INS_ACCSCAL_Y 1.001
INS_ACCSCAL_Z 1.001
INS_ACC2OFFS_X 0.001
INS_ACC2OFFS_Y 0.001
INS_ACC2OFFS_Z 0.001
INS_ACC2SCAL_X 1.001
INS_ACC2SCAL_Y 1.001
INS_ACC2SCAL_Z 1.001

INS_ACCEL_FILTER 10
INS_ENABLE_MASK 127
INS_FAST_SAMPLE 3
INS_GYR_CAL 1
INS_GYRO_FILTER 20
INS_GYRO_RATE 1
# Their notch kept: it tracks throttle alone, needs no sensor SITL lacks, and their gains were tuned with its phase lag in the loop.
# REF 1 = full throttle, HMNCS 2 = 2nd harmonic only: 116*sqrt(throttle)*2, about 133 Hz at hover, the 2-blade pass rate.
INS_HNTCH_ATT 40
INS_HNTCH_BW 58
INS_HNTCH_ENABLE 1
INS_HNTCH_FM_RAT 1
INS_HNTCH_FREQ 116
INS_HNTCH_HMNCS 2
INS_HNTCH_MODE 1
INS_HNTCH_REF 1
INS_RAW_LOG_OPT 9
INS_STILL_THRESH 2.5
INS_TRIM_OPTION 1
INS_USE 1
INS_USE2 1
INS_USE3 0

# Theirs: LAND_ALT_LOW 500, LAND_SPEED 30
LAND_ALT_LOW_M 5
LAND_SPD_MS 0.3
LAND_REPOSITION 1
LOG_BACKEND_TYPE 1
LOG_BITMASK 407550
LOG_FILE_BUFSIZE 200
LOG_FILE_DSRMROT 1
LOG_FILE_MB_FREE 500
LOG_MAX_FILES 500
# Theirs: LOIT_ACC_MAX 250, LOIT_BRK_ACCEL 220, LOIT_BRK_JERK 500, LOIT_SPEED 1250
LOIT_ACC_MAX_M 2.5
LOIT_BRK_ACC_M 2.2
LOIT_BRK_JRK_M 5
LOIT_SPEED_MS 12.5
LOIT_BRK_DELAY 0.4
LOIT_OPTIONS 1

# Motors: theirs. Controls.xml maps their 1050..1950 us onto the ESC map's 0..1.
MOT_BAT_VOLT_MAX 60.9
MOT_BAT_VOLT_MIN 46.2
MOT_HOVER_LEARN 2
MOT_PWM_MAX 1950
MOT_PWM_MIN 1050
# Theirs is 10, which ArduPilot does not define (0..9) and DroneCAN ignores; SITL sends plain PWM to the simulator.
MOT_PWM_TYPE 0
MOT_SAFE_TIME 1
MOT_SPIN_ARM 0.07
MOT_SPIN_MAX 0.95
MOT_SPIN_MIN 0.1
MOT_SPOOL_TIME 0.5
# Theirs, kept as their config. The Hobbywing table fits 0.27 and this JSBSim model 0.29.
MOT_THST_EXPO 0.74
MOT_YAW_HEADROOM 200

OA_TYPE 0
# Theirs: PILOT_ACCEL_Z 250, PILOT_SPEED_UP 250
PILOT_ACC_Z 2.5
PILOT_SPD_UP 2.5
RCMAP_PITCH 2
RCMAP_ROLL 1
RCMAP_THROTTLE 3
RCMAP_YAW 4
# Theirs: RTL_ALT 1000, RTL_ALT_FINAL 0
RTL_ALT_M 10
RTL_ALT_FINAL_M 0
# Theirs is 1, terrain, which their radar altimeter serves. Without one ArduCopter wants terrain tiles from a GCS before it arms
# (AP_Arming_Copter::terrain_database_required), and SRTM tiles are not the PteroSim scene anyway.
RTL_ALT_TYPE 0
RTL_CONE_SLOPE 3
RTL_LOIT_TIME 5000
SCHED_LOOP_RATE 400
SERIAL0_BAUD 115
SERIAL0_PROTOCOL 2
# SITL's SERIAL1/2 are TCP 5762/5763; MAVLink2 there as on their telemetry radios.
SERIAL1_BAUD 57
SERIAL1_OPTIONS 0
SERIAL1_PROTOCOL 2
SERIAL2_BAUD 57
SERIAL2_OPTIONS 0
SERIAL2_PROTOCOL 2
SERVO_RATE 50
SERVO1_FUNCTION 33
SERVO1_MAX 1950
SERVO1_MIN 1050
SERVO1_TRIM 1500
SERVO2_FUNCTION 34
SERVO2_MAX 1950
SERVO2_MIN 1050
SERVO2_TRIM 1500
SERVO3_FUNCTION 35
SERVO3_MAX 1950
SERVO3_MIN 1050
SERVO3_TRIM 1500
SERVO4_FUNCTION 36
SERVO4_MAX 1950
SERVO4_MIN 1050
SERVO4_TRIM 1500

# Sim only, not Arrow's: their file sets no mount. The SIYI A8 mini as a servo mount (MNT1_TYPE 1) on SERVO5-7, which are
# Controls.xml channels 4-6, so a mission's DO_SET_ROI aims it. Each MIN/MAX is the binding's out=; the full PWM span,
# as the simulator reads (PWM - 1500) / 500. MNT1_DEFLT_MODE 2: MAVLink targeting while no ROI is set.
MNT1_TYPE 1
MNT1_DEFLT_MODE 2
MNT1_ROLL_MIN -45
MNT1_ROLL_MAX 45
MNT1_PITCH_MIN -90
MNT1_PITCH_MAX 90
MNT1_YAW_MIN -180
MNT1_YAW_MAX 180
SERVO5_FUNCTION 8
SERVO6_FUNCTION 7
SERVO7_FUNCTION 6
SERVO5_MIN 1000
SERVO5_MAX 2000
SERVO6_MIN 1000
SERVO6_MAX 2000
SERVO7_MIN 1000
SERVO7_MAX 2000
TERRAIN_ENABLE 1
TERRAIN_SPACING 100
THR_DZ 100
# Theirs: WPNAV_ACCEL 100, WPNAV_ACCEL_Z 50, WPNAV_JERK 1, WPNAV_RADIUS 25, WPNAV_RFND_USE 1, WPNAV_SPEED 350, WPNAV_SPEED_DN 100,
# WPNAV_SPEED_UP 100. The group is WP_ now; JERK and RFND_USE kept their units.
WP_ACC 1
WP_ACC_Z 0.5
WP_JERK 1
WP_RADIUS_M 0.25
WP_RFND_USE 1
WP_SPD 3.5
WP_SPD_DN 1
WP_SPD_UP 1

# Left out, SITL has no such hardware:
#   CAN_D1_*, CAN_D2_*, CAN_P1_*, CAN_P2_*   DroneCAN buses, ESC bitmask included: SITL's SERVO1-4 outputs drive the motors
#   BATT_OPTIONS 128, BATT2_MONITOR 9        DroneCAN battery-node option and a second CAN monitor
#   GPS2_TYPE 9, GPS2_GNSS_MODE, GPS2_RATE_MS  second DroneCAN receiver
#   RNGFND1_*                                NanoRadar on CAN; PteroSim sends SITL no range (no rng_N in its JSON)
#   PRX_FILT, PRX1_*, SERIAL5_*              RPLidar S2L on SERIAL5; not simulated, and proximity with no data fails arming
#   SERIAL3_BAUD/OPTIONS, SERIAL4_*          SERIAL3/4 are SITL's simulated GPS ports, not their companion links
#   BRD_*, SERVO_GPIO_MASK, NTF_LED_*        Pixhawk board: safety switch, watchdog, USB voltage, GPIO pins, LEDs
#   NET_ENABLE 0                             Ethernet bridge to the Pi (0 is the default)
# Compass offsets stay at zero: SITL's simulated ones are zero (SIM_MAG1_OFS default).
